title: "Nonnegative Runge–Kutta coefficients do not make modified Patankar schemes globally stable: a counterexample with attracting two-cycles"
type: software
authors:
  - name: Anonymous
version: 1.0.1-candidate
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23511175
date-released: 2026-10-20
repository-code: "https://github.com/ipitchford/mprk-nonnegative-two-cycles"
url: "https://evidencepress.org/releases/mprk-nonnegative-two-cycles/"
license: CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - modified Patankar–Runge–Kutta schemes
  - positivity-preserving time integration
  - global stability
  - spurious periodic orbits
  - computer-assisted proof
abstract: "Counterexample to the natural universal reading of the Izgin–Kopecz–Meister–Schilling conjecture: MPRK22(4/7), with all nonzero tableau coefficients positive, has a certified attracting two-cycle on a stiff two-species linear system although the steady state is the unique positive fixed point and locally stable. Includes the complete phase portrait, parameter ranges, three-species and third-order examples, global convergence proofs for alpha = 1/2 and alpha = 1 (two species), and exact interval-arithmetic verifiers. Unrefereed, AI-assisted candidate. Original code is MIT-licensed; see LICENSES.md."
